# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Home Lab Dashboard — service connections
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in what you have. Every service is optional:
# the dashboard shows a neutral "not connected" tile for anything missing and
# keeps working, so you can wire these up one at a time.
#
# ADDRESSES: if the dashboard runs on the SAME machine as your services (the
# usual case) and you use the provided docker-compose.yml, it runs with host
# networking — so use http://127.0.0.1:<port>. That keeps traffic on the box
# and avoids the host firewall entirely.
#
# Only use LAN addresses (http://192.168.x.x:port) when the dashboard runs on a
# DIFFERENT machine than the services. In that case the firewall on the
# services box has to allow this machine.
#
# These are read server-side only — no key is ever sent to the browser.
#
# After editing, restart the dev server, then open /setup to test.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Plex Media Server — default port 32400
# Token: open any library item → ⋮ → Get Info → View XML, copy X-Plex-Token
# from the address bar.
PLEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:32400
PLEX_TOKEN=

# Tautulli — default port 8181
# Key: Settings → Web Interface → API key
TAUTULLI_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8181
TAUTULLI_API_KEY=

# Sonarr — default port 8989
# Key: Settings → General → API Key
SONARR_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8989
SONARR_API_KEY=

# Radarr — default port 7878
# Key: Settings → General → API Key
RADARR_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7878
RADARR_API_KEY=

# Bazarr — default port 6767
# Key: Settings → General → API Key
BAZARR_URL=http://127.0.0.1:6767
BAZARR_API_KEY=

# Glances — default port 61208. No API key.
# Run it on the server with the compose service in docker-compose.yml.
GLANCES_URL=http://127.0.0.1:61208
# Glances 4 is current; set to 3 for older installs. The client probes both,
# so this is only a hint.
GLANCES_API_VERSION=4

# Filename for the library-size history (JSON Lines), stored in ./data/.
# Delete the file to reset the growth chart.
HISTORY_FILE=history.jsonl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mute health checks that don't apply to your setup.
#
# A dashboard permanently showing warnings you've decided not to care about is
# worse than one showing none — you stop reading the panel, and the real
# warning hiding among them goes unnoticed. Muted checks are still COUNTED in
# the health panel, so a rule can't quietly hide something later.
#
# Matching is on the check's source (Servarr's stable check-class name), not
# its message, since messages carry version numbers and get reworded.
#
# Comma-separated. Each entry is one of:
#   download-automation   named group: indexer + download-client + import checks
#   updates               named group: "new update is available"
#   IndexerRssCheck       one check source, on every service
#   sonarr:UpdateCheck    one check source, on one service only
#
# Ripping discs rather than using indexers and a download client? This clears
# the whole permanently-true family:
# HEALTH_MUTE=download-automation

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alerts — get told, instead of having to look.
#
# Fires when a mount crosses 90%, a service goes unreachable, an import stalls,
# a pool member fills while the pool still looks healthy, or a sensor passes
# its critical temperature.
#
# Edge-triggered with hysteresis and a repeat interval, and the known-active
# set is persisted, so a full disk notifies once rather than every few seconds
# — and a container restart doesn't re-announce what you already know.
#
# ntfy: install the app, pick an unguessable topic name, subscribe to it.
# ALERT_NTFY_URL=https://ntfy.sh/your-unguessable-topic-name
# ALERT_NTFY_TOKEN=            # only for a protected/self-hosted ntfy

# Any webhook receiver; the payload is Discord-compatible.
# ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# "warning" (default) or "critical" to only hear about the serious ones.
# ALERT_MIN_LEVEL=warning

# Hours before a still-true condition reminds you. 0 disables reminders.
# ALERT_REPEAT_HOURS=12

# Where this dashboard is reachable. Makes notifications tappable: the Discord
# embed title links here, and ntfy gets a Click action, both deep-linked to the
# page the alert concerns (/storage for a full disk, /health for a dead
# service). Use the Tailscale name if you have one.
# DASHBOARD_URL=https://steven-plex.your-tailnet.ts.net

# Payload shape. Auto-detected from the hostname; force it only if something
# speaks Discord's format behind a different host (a proxy or relay).
# ALERT_WEBHOOK_FORMAT=auto     # auto | discord | generic
